  "chapter": {
    "number": 138,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(139) For the end, a Psalm of David.",
          {
            "noteId": 245
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "O Lord, you have proved me, and known me.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You know my down-sitting and my up-rising: you understand my thoughts",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 246
          },
          {
            "text": "long before.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You have traced my path and my",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 247
          },
          {
            "text": "bed, and have foreseen all my ways.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For there is no unrighteous word in my tongue: behold, O Lord, you have known all things,",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "the last and the first: you have fashioned me, and laid your hand upon me.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The knowledge of you is too wonderful for me; it is very difficult, I can’t attain to it.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Whither shall I go from your Spirit? and whither shall I flee from your presence?",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "If I should go up to heaven, you are there: if I should go down to hell, you are present.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "If I should spread my wings to fly",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 248
          },
          {
            "text": "straight forward, and sojourn at the extremity of the sea, it would be vain,",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "for even there your hand would guide me, and your right hand would hold me.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "When I said, Surely the darkness will cover me; even the night was light in my",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 249
          },
          {
            "text": "luxury.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 12,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For darkness will not be darkness with you; but night will be light as day: as its darkness, so shall its light be to you.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 13,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For you, O Lord, have possessed my reins; you have helped me from my mother's womb.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 14,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I will give you thanks; for you are fearfully wondrous; wondrous are your works; and my soul knows it well.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 15,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "My bones, which you made in secret were not hidden from you, nor my substance, in the lowest parts of the earth.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 16,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Your eyes saw my unwrought substance, and all men shall be written in your book; they shall be formed by day, though there should for a time be no one among them.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 17,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "But your friends, O God, have been greatly honored by me; their rule has been greatly strengthened.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 18,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I will number them, and they shall be multiplied beyond the sand; I awake, and am still with you.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 19,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Oh that you would kill the wicked, O God; depart from me, you⌃ men of blood.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 20,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For you will say concerning their thought, that they shall take your cities in vain.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 21,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Have I not hated them, O Lord, that hate you? and wasted away because of your enemies?",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 22,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I have hated them with perfect hatred; they were counted my enemies.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 23,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Prove me, O God, and know my heart; examine me, and know my paths;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 24,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "and see if there is any way of iniquity in me, and lead me in an everlasting way.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
